course: dictionary
lesson: 4220
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word grade has several meanings, so context tells you which one. «Maya is in third grade» is about a school year. «She got good grades» is about the marks she earned for her work.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Josh's story says, «his marks dropped a whole grade», so his school marks went down one level. Swap in a word like level or mark, and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Grade can also be a verb. «The teacher will grade our tests» means she will give marks to our work. Sometimes a grade is about steepness too: «the road has a steep grade» means the road goes up sharply.
fact: A grade can be a school year or class, like second grade. This is mostly used in the USA and Canada; the UK says Year 2.
fact: A grade can be a mark for your work, like a letter from A to F or a score on a test.
fact: A grade can be a level of how good or strong something is, like «grade A eggs».
fact: To grade means to give marks to work, or to sort things by size or quality.
fact: A grade is also how steep a road or slope is.
exercise: «Maya is in second grade now.» What does grade mean here? | A way of sorting eggs | A letter mark for work | *A school year or class | A steep slope
exercise: «The road up the hill has a steep grade.» What does grade mean? | To give marks to work | A level of quality | A school year | *How steep a road or slope is
exercise: «"OtsInka" means a mark or grade; in Ukrainian schools marks run from 1 to 12, and 12 is the best.» What is the best mark? | *12 | 1 | 6 | 10
test: «Ms Lee will grade our maths tests on Friday.» What does grade mean here? | A level of how strong something is | To climb a steep hill | *To give marks to work | A school year
test: «A boy in Scotland became so tired that he fell asleep in class and his grades dropped.» What do grades mean here? | How steep a hill is | *Marks for school work | Years at school | Types of honey
exam: «"Not yet" used as a grade (US) means fail.» What does "Not yet" mean as a grade in the USA? | Excellent | *Fail | Ask the teacher again | Pass
